              <p class="!mb-0"><strong>In short:</strong> Mixing balances the individual tracks in your recording — adjusting levels, EQ, compression, and effects so everything works together. Mastering is the final stage that polishes the complete stereo mix, sets loudness for streaming, and prepares files for release. They are separate processes, done in sequence, on different file types.</p>
